cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SAUT, or build on the concepts it implements (cross-harness
  privilege semantics for the agent surface of a repository, the
  always-on/on-invoke cost passport, and trigger/obedience measurement
  across harnesses), please cite it as below.
title: "SAUT: Surface Assurance Under Trust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuriy
    family-names: Orlov
    email: yuriy.orlov@undertrust.dev
abstract: >-
  SAUT is an assurance tool for the agent surface of a repository: the
  skills, subagents, MCP servers, hooks, settings, permissions and
  instruction files an AI coding agent loads or runs from it. It reports
  what no single harness will tell you: per harness, whether the declared tool allowlist
  is a restriction, a pre-approval grant, informational prose or a field
  dropped on render; what the artifact costs in every session versus on
  invocation; and, by compiling it into a scratch workspace and running
  each harness headlessly, whether the harness fires it and
  whether the run stays inside the declaration it made. The recorded
  semantics is data with provenance, and the bench measures it rather
  than asserting it.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agentic-coding
  - agent-skills
  - agent-surface
  - mcp
  - static-analysis
  - evaluation
  - token-budget
  - least-privilege
  - claude-code
  - codex
  - opencode
repository-code: "https://github.com/yurgeno/saut"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.10.0
date-released: '2026-11-15'
